WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.934
-Our next guest can be seen
at the Historic Everett Theatre

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:06.634
in Everett, Washington,
this Saturday night.

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:09.400
Please welcome
the very funny Jackie Fabulous!

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:19.133
♪♪

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:21.167
-Hey, guys. What's up?

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:22.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.234 --> 00:00:25.567
Oh, I have so many milestones
to share.

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:30.400
I'm about to have really
high self-esteem this summer.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.534
I'm going to Jamaica
to see my relatives.

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:35.400
Yeah! Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.901
I tell women, if you want
to know how good you look,

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:40.434
how hot you are, go to
the Caribbean, any island.

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:43.434
You'll know how you look. Okay?
I'm very self-aware.

00:00:43.434 --> 00:00:45.801
I know I'm like a life-sized
Cabbage Patch Doll.

00:00:45.801 --> 00:00:47.267
I get it, right?

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:50.234
I used to live in California.
On that man scale of 1 to 10,

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:52.934
I know I'm a 6.
I get it, right?

00:00:52.934 --> 00:00:55.701
In New York, I'm an 8.
I can cook. Y'all like that.

00:00:55.701 --> 00:00:57.968
Okay? [ Laughs ]

00:00:57.968 --> 00:01:00.434
But in Jamaica, I'm Beyoncé.

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:01.834
Okay?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:05.200
I am a 49.6 in Jamaica.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:06.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:06.501 --> 00:01:09.267
Okay?

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:10.667
I can't walk around.

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:12.734
It's not safe for me
to walk around in Jamaica.

00:01:12.734 --> 00:01:15.734
Okay? And here's the thing.
I was working on a comedy cruise

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:17.334
and we had a port stop
in Jamaica.

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:18.567
I went for a walk.

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:20.067
Right? You shouldn't
do that by yourself.

00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:24.634
And this man my age
chasing me on a bike.

00:01:24.634 --> 00:01:26.367
A bike!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:28.334
And he's like, "Baby girl, where
are you going?

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:30.834
Let me show you the island."

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:32.834
I'm like,
"How? On your handlebars, sir?

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:36.067
How are you going
to show me anything?"

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:37.934
And another man running
after me, he's like,

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:39.100
"So where do you work?"

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.968
I said, "I work on the boat
there part time."

00:01:40.968 --> 00:01:42.367
He's like, "Part time?

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:44.400
You give me your body,
I'll work on it full time."

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.868
I'm like, "Oh, okay.
Alright. I like it here."

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:50.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:51.934
Speaking of confidence,

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:54.767
I officially permanently moved
out of my mother's house.

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:56.067
Give it up for me. Yes.

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:57.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:57.601 --> 00:01:59.033
Yeah.

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:01.901
You shouldn't clap. I'm 51.
That's sad. I shouldn't...

00:02:01.901 --> 00:02:03.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.934 --> 00:02:06.834
And I'm going to miss my
mother's sweet, sweet judgment.

00:02:06.834 --> 00:02:09.767
I'm going to miss her judgment.
She hates this job.

00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:12.734
Her exact words were, "Jackie,
you know I hate comedy."

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:14.334
I don't know. That's like saying
you don't like joy.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.400
I don't get it.
But she loves discussing

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.634
what I do with my neighbors
when I move back home.

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:19.701
Neighbors are nosy.
They're like,

00:02:19.701 --> 00:02:21.868
"So what do you do
for a living now?"

00:02:21.868 --> 00:02:23.033
My mom jumped in.

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:24.634
"Jackie is a joke!"

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:30.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:33.067
She's like, "You know the card,
the funny man on the card,

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:34.400
the joker? That's Jackie."

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:35.567
I said, "Mommy, that's correct.

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:38.167
But what I do,
I'm called a comedian."

00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:40.667
She's like, "Do you
tell jokes for money?"

00:02:40.667 --> 00:02:43.567
Well, yes.
"Do you have a law degree?"

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:45.868
Yes, ma'am.
"Then you're a freaking joke."

00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:47.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:50.167
Yeah.

00:02:50.167 --> 00:02:52.467
I'm going to miss that.

00:02:52.467 --> 00:02:54.968
I'm going to miss her
weather reports every day.

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:57.200
Right? Because I used
to live in Cali.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.567
I don't miss inclement weather.

00:02:58.567 --> 00:03:02.467
She's like, "Jackie, you know it
rained on Monday.

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:06.200
Jacqueline, you know
it rained on Tuesday.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.767
Jackie, you will not believe
this. It rained on Wednesday."

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:10.968
I get it, Mommy.
We share the same TV. I get it.

00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:11.868
I can see what you see.

00:03:11.868 --> 00:03:13.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.367 --> 00:03:16.467
I'm going to miss her very heavy
Jamaican accent, right?

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:18.868
She loves reality TV.
She would call me to discuss.

00:03:18.868 --> 00:03:21.133
I don't know what show
she's talking about, right?

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:23.667
She's like, "Jackie,
I love that show Ardas.

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:26.334
The show on TV,
and the show is called Ardas.

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:29.200
And the lady on the show
has 85 pussies."

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:34.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.601 --> 00:03:36.834
I'm like, "What show
are you watching, Mommy?"

00:03:36.834 --> 00:03:38.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.834 --> 00:03:41.100
And I'm like, "Wait a minute.
You mean 'Hoarders'?"

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:42.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:44.567
The lady with 85 cats?

00:03:44.567 --> 00:03:46.467
Your accent is jacked up.
I'm sorry.

00:03:46.467 --> 00:03:47.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.767 --> 00:03:49.834
And FYI, they don't
call them that word anywhere.

00:03:49.834 --> 00:03:51.834
They're called cats in
every country. I've checked.

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:56.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.033 --> 00:03:58.467
Another big milestone
since I was here last --

00:03:58.467 --> 00:04:00.267
I got married! Yeah!

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:01.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:05.467
Love! Yes.

00:04:05.467 --> 00:04:08.300
And I'm obnoxious.
You know, six months married.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.400
I'm an expert, right?

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.767
So on Instagram,
pictures of he and I

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:14.534
and I'm getting DMs from women
now who want advice.

00:04:14.534 --> 00:04:16.567
They're like, "Jack,"
because I married an ex-athlete,

00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:18.701
ex-jock, you know,
a hot guy with muscles.

00:04:18.701 --> 00:04:21.734
And they're like, "Jackie, how
did you find love at your age?

00:04:21.734 --> 00:04:23.801
How did you find him?"
I'm real.

00:04:23.801 --> 00:04:26.167
You got to find man
when they're at the end, okay?

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:27.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:30.000
The more these guys'
bodies fall apart,

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.868
the more they want
to commit to you. Alright?

00:04:31.868 --> 00:04:33.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:35.801
When my husband's
left knee blew out,

00:04:35.801 --> 00:04:37.934
he's like, "Jackie,
I have always loved you."

00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:39.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.934 --> 00:04:42.200
When the right knee died,
"we should get married."

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.868
I'm not a fool.
Men get lonely, too.

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:47.934
You don't want to die alone.
I get it, you know.

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:49.734
But the one thing
we don't have in common

00:04:49.734 --> 00:04:51.467
is that, you know,
the athlete who can cook.

00:04:51.467 --> 00:04:53.567
We started dating,
and in the beginning of it,

00:04:53.567 --> 00:04:55.334
at 12:30, midnight, he was like,

00:04:55.334 --> 00:04:59.801
"So, um, do you want
a meatball sandwich?"

00:04:59.801 --> 00:05:02.501
I'm like,
"It is 12:00 at night."

00:05:02.501 --> 00:05:04.434
And he's like -- And I'm like,
"Of course I do."

00:05:04.434 --> 00:05:05.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.534 --> 00:05:06.701
That's part of the problem.

00:05:06.701 --> 00:05:08.133
But I'm feeling guilty.

00:05:08.133 --> 00:05:10.601
When you have a hot guy who
lives in the gym, good shape,

00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:14.133
you know, I'm not going to lie.
All this newlywed new stuff.

00:05:14.133 --> 00:05:15.868
You know what I'm talking about.
I feel like --

00:05:15.868 --> 00:05:17.868
I feel like he's killing me.
I feel like I'm dying.

00:05:17.868 --> 00:05:20.601
Like I have a hernia
or a slipped disc.

00:05:20.601 --> 00:05:23.667
I know when you go from nothing
to all of this, it's a lot.

00:05:23.667 --> 00:05:25.701
Right?
And I'm worried.

00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:27.133
I don't want him
to have a heart attack.

00:05:27.133 --> 00:05:28.601
You can't have the person
in good shape

00:05:28.601 --> 00:05:30.434
doing all the work
all the time.

00:05:30.434 --> 00:05:31.968
He's always taking the lead
in the bedroom.

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:33.300
I'm like, "You know what?
I got to take the lead"

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:34.667
and give it to him
when he gives me.

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.400
So I decided to show him

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.300
that I can love him
the way he loves me.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:41.200
So I did. Two weeks ago,
I gave him a great time.

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:43.067
I had been in pain
for two weeks.

00:05:43.067 --> 00:05:45.067
[ Laughter ]
I have been talking

00:05:45.067 --> 00:05:47.767
and making jokes
about men's stamina for years.

00:05:47.767 --> 00:05:49.834
I apologize. Okay?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.834 --> 00:05:51.434
I tried to do what you guys did.

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:53.601
I couldn't get through.
I needed a five-minute break.

00:05:53.601 --> 00:05:58.334
[ Laughter ]
A granola bar, a Red Bull.

00:05:58.334 --> 00:06:01.033
In the middle of it, I'm looking
for excuses to get a break.

00:06:01.033 --> 00:06:03.901
I'm like, "You don't hear
that noise downstairs?

00:06:03.901 --> 00:06:05.100
You don't want to go check?"

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:11.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:11.834 --> 00:06:13.934
I'm like, "You're not hot?
You don't feel warm?

00:06:13.934 --> 00:06:16.834
It's stuffy in here.

00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:18.634
I smell smoke.
I don't feel safe."

00:06:18.634 --> 00:06:20.400
[ Laughter ]
"There's a fire somewhere."

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.901
I'm Jackie Fabulous.
Thank you so much, guys.

00:06:22.901 --> 00:06:26.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:26.334 --> 00:06:28.968
-Are you kidding me now?
Are you kidding me?

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:32.701
Jackie Fabulous!

00:06:32.701 --> 00:06:33.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:33.934 --> 00:06:37.133
You're awesome.
See Jackie this Saturday night

00:06:37.133 --> 00:06:40.734
at the Historic Everett Theatre
in Everett, Washington.

00:06:40.734 --> 00:06:42.968
We'll be right back,
everybody. Come on back.

